<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>MUI.I3</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>MUI.I3</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    No reference to MUI.Catalog, for the same reason MUI.Crawl has none: what comes back off this
    socket is raw observation, and turning it into catalogue state belongs to whatever assembles a
    reading. The arrow stays one-way so every downstream writer is testable against a captured reply
    with no gateway and no network in sight (spec §6.5, §13).

    No reference to MUI.Crawl either, and that is not an oversight. An I3 count and a telnet probe
    are two separate observations of the same game arriving at different moments down different
    pipes; nothing here belongs inside a ProbeResult.
  -->

</Project>
